From af8763d03b01f834244af91a0d378cdcc39da628 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeffrey Hutchins <complife@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 11:53:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] feat(ringback): replace ringback asset with generated
 US PSTN tone (#6)

* feat(ringback): replace ringback asset with generated US PSTN tone

The shipped ringtone.wav was not a ringback tone. It was a 2.11s stereo
44.1kHz percussive sample whose envelope decayed to silence by ~1.4s, with
its energy around 400Hz -- looped, it produced a repeating blip rather than
ringing. Both platforms played it; Android has played it for years.

Replace it on iOS and Android with the US Precise Tone Plan ringback:
440Hz + 480Hz summed, 2s on / 4s off, one full 6s cadence so the players'
existing loop reproduces the cadence. Mono 16kHz 16-bit PCM.

Generated by scripts/generate-ringback-tone.py (stdlib wave + math) rather
than vendored, so the tone is reproducible instead of an opaque binary.
2.000s is a whole number of cycles at both frequencies, so the tone starts
and ends at zero phase and the loop point is seamless.

R.raw.ringtone is used only by MediaPlayerManager.startRingback(); the
incoming ringtone is R.raw.incoming and is untouched.

* fix(ios): stop ringback on provider reset and resume after interruption

Two pre-existing failure modes in the ringback path, both silent.

providerDidReset: disabled the audio device but left the looping player
running. A CallKit reset orphans the TVOCall, so no didDisconnect fires
and callDisconnected: -- the usual caller of stopRingback -- never runs.
The tone then loops forever with no call behind it. callMap is left
populated on purpose; it is the sole strong reference to live TVOCalls
and clearing it without disconnecting them is a behavioral change.

playRingback registered no AVAudioSessionInterruptionNotification
observer. AVAudioPlayer pauses on interruption and never resumes itself,
so an incoming cellular or FaceTime call mid-ring killed the tone for
the remainder of the ring with no error and no log. Resume on .Ended
when the options carry ShouldResume, and log via RCTLogError on the
paths where the tone is genuinely lost. The observer is removed by name
in stopRingback so it cannot outlive the player, and so it cannot tear
down the push-registry and route-change observers this object also holds.

